A||||10||Klown||Shifting Techniques||||1||
Z||000000||Klown||03-26-2000||05:20 AM||||I was hoping the members of the forum could offer their advice on shifting techniques to get the best acceleration.  I'd especially like to know what RPM to launch at and what RPM to shift at with a manual transmission and a basically stock engine.    ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||03-26-2000||09:13 PM||||push in the clutch when you shift!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||03-26-2000||10:24 PM||||let the clutch out when its in the next gear!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||03-26-2000||10:59 PM||||I'm sorry, its a pack instinct kind of thing.<P>I launch my GT at thiry five hundred and shift at fifty five.  Also eat clutches like they were soft ice cream.  A good exhaust should push the shift points higher, at least I'm counting on that.||||reg||12
Z||000004||Klown||03-27-2000||04:23 AM||||Is it true I have to move that "stick" looking thing coming out of the center console to select the gears or is that just optional...LOL||||reg||10
Z||000005||Dan86gt3.8||03-27-2000||05:13 AM||||I put mine in od and hit the gas, and I let this machine do the shifting for me, and man is it great.||||reg||12
Z||000006||TalShino||03-27-2000||08:16 AM||||Ya'll got some strange ones here. Really ya do. Odd Odd Odd ppl. But alas, I'm one of em so cool. hehe.. <P>Ray -TalShino||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||03-27-2000||08:22 AM||||5,500 rpm is probably past the power peak of a stock engine. 5,000 is probably a better shift point. You probably should experiment with your own launch rpm. You want to find the highest engine speed that will get you going WITHOUT spinning the tires (if you lost traction, it's too much). That'll depend a little on the kind of tires and clutch you have.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||03-27-2000||09:28 AM||||Launch my car nitrous on AND off at 1300. Less wheel spin and don't have the wheel hop problems. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>  and shift at about 5300.. that keeps me in my broadest torque curve which keeps me pulling hard and not falling on my face in the top end. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Patrick's Dad||03-27-2000||11:39 PM||||Hmmm...<P>According to my son (3½YO), instructing my wife on how to drive Daddy's Car (She doesn't know how to drive a stick), "You just move the big circle and drive."||||reg||10
Z||000010||Phaeton||03-28-2000||03:49 AM||||3500 RPM keeps the engine about max torque and the clutch keeps the tires at the edge of breaking loose.  For years I have thought this was an efficient use of the clutch and it gives phenomenal acceleration.<P>But thinking back on those blue flywheels with little canyons everywhere is starting to make me go 'Hmmmmmmm'||||reg||12
